Consider the following scheme for implementing a critical section in a situation with three processes $P_i$, $P_j$ and $P_k$.

```pascal
Pi:
repeat
  flag[i] := true;
  while flag[j] or flag[k] do
    case turn of
      j: if flag[j] then
         begin
           flag[i] := false;
           while turn <> i do skip;
           flag[i] := true
         end;
      k: if flag[k] then
         begin
           flag[i] := false;
           while turn <> i do skip;
           flag[i] := true
         end
    end;
  critical section
  if turn = i then turn := j;
  flag[i] := false;
  non-critical section
until false;
```

Does the scheme ensure mutual exclusion in the critical section? Briefly explain.

